"Clear to his marrow&mdash;does more thinking and reading on that subject than
                any other except Russia and Siberia: thrashes around over the whole field, too;
                nothing bigoted about him."

"We've got him, Major&mdash;got him sure! I've seen him&mdash;seen him good;
                and I don't care where or when that man approaches me backwards, I'll recognize
                him every time. We're all right. Now for the requisition."

Presently one of the gaping and adoring half-circle of boys ventured a timid
                question. My lord answered it. The boys glanced wonderingly at each other and
                from somewhere fell the comment:

"<i>Don't!</i> There's just pure heart-break in that tone. It's just as I say;
                you've got to get right down to it and amuse your mind, as if it was
                salvation."

"Yes, he certainly is great in that feature, one is obliged to admit it;
                but&mdash;now mind, I'm not really criticising&mdash;don't you think he is just
                a trifle overstrong in technique?"

O, <i>how</i> the boarders yell,<br />
                When they hear that dinner bell<br />
                They give that landlord&mdash;

Sellers, pale and a good deal agitated, opened the door and confronted Tracy.
                The old man could not at once get his voice: then he pumped out a scattering
                and hardly coherent salutation, and followed it with&mdash;

Said the Colonel to himself, "This phantom lies like an expert. Purifying this
                kind by fire don't work. I'll sound him a little further, give him another
                chance or two to work his gift." Then aloud&mdash;with deep irony&mdash;

It was as far as she could get. There was a pause; his intellect was struggling
                to comprehend; presently it did manage to catch the idea in time to save
                embarrassment all around, and he said gratefully&mdash;

That head still drooped! Sally rose, moved softly and solemnly a step or two,
                and stood before Tracy&mdash;his head came slowly up, his meek eyes met her
                intense ones&mdash;then she finished with deep impressiveness&mdash;

Slowly and painfully the statesman worked the truth into his head that this was
                really a flesh and blood young man, and not the insubstantial resurrection he
